    "q-213365": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213365",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe integer $34$ \n{{field-1}}\nthe additive inverse of $18$ modulo $48$ since $34+18$ {{field-2}} $(\\text{mod}\\,48).$",
      "worked_solution": "The additive inverse of $18$ modulo $48$ is the integer $0\\le x<48$ such that\n\n$$\nx+18≡0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,48).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that when we add our two numbers, we get a number that is *not* congruent to zero modulo $48:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}34+18 & ≡52 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≡48+4 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≡4 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48) \\\\  & ≢0 & \\,(\\text{mod}\\,48)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude the following:\n\nThe integer $34$ $\\text{is not}$ the additive inverse of $18$ modulo $48$ since $34+18≢0\\,(\\text{mod}\\,48).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
